LUNA uses braindecode's own `return_features`, phase fix and `reset_head` (braindecode #1565, #1566, #1568) instead of coco-pipe's patch of its frequency embedding and forward hook on its final norm; the embeddings are the same. LUNA therefore needs braindecode 2.1, `main` until it is released. CI runs the tests that need mne-bids or braindecode `main` in one job on both.
EEGPT loads through braindecode's `from_pretrained` on the input channels, without a channel projection, instead of coco-pipe's own loader: it finds each channel's embedding by name, and loads every checkpoint tensor on a subset of its 62 channels with braindecode 2.0 and `main` alike. The embeddings are the same.
